<title>GERMANY: LAMFALUSSY SAYS EMU STABILITY PACT A GOOD IDEA.</title>
<headline>LAMFALUSSY SAYS EMU STABILITY PACT A GOOD IDEA.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-08-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Alexandre Lamfalussy, president of the European Monetary Institute, said on Tuesday a stability pact for long-term compliance with budget and debt criteria in Europe's planned currency union was a good idea.</p>
<p>&quot;In this field the view is simple. A stability pact would be very useful,&quot; Lamfalussy said, adding it would be needed in the long run.</p>
<p>Lamfalussy said the European Monetary Institute would not give specific advice to nations' finance ministers but that it does extend its general blessing to such a pact.</p>
<p>&quot;The finance ministers are the ones who have to produce it (the stability pact),&quot; he said.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom + 49 69 756525</p>
</text>
